    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task was to expose a `timezone` field on the owner response, derived from the owner's locality/region via the fixed table `NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`, as an IANA name.\n\nFollowing the existing `locality` pattern, I made three changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/java/.../util/Locality.java`** \u2014 added a `REGION_TIMEZONE` map and a public `timezone(String region)` method that returns the IANA name (or `null` for an unknown region, e.g. `UNKNOWN`).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `timezone`, deriving it from the same region that feeds `locality`: `Locality.timezone(CustomerCode.region(owner.getCustomerCode()))`.\n\n3. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `timezone` string property to the Owner schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` test (Sydney \u2192 NSW \u2192 `Australia/Sydney`) passes, and the full `./mvnw test` run reports **BUILD SUCCESS** with 0 failures/errors.",
